    "result_text": "Build passes \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` is green, and the audit log confirms distinct codes are generated.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customer-code de-duplication so that when a computed `customerCode` collides with an existing owner's, `-<n>` is appended using the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\nThe logic is split cleanly across the layers, following the existing `findByTelephone` / `findByEmailIgnoreCase` duplicate-detection idiom:\n\n- **`CustomerCodeGenerator.deduplicate(baseCode, takenCodes)`** \u2014 pure code-arithmetic: returns `baseCode` when free, else scans `baseCode-2`, `baseCode-3`, \u2026 for the first not taken. Lives with the code-building logic it belongs to.\n- **`OwnerRepository.findByCustomerCodeStartingWith(prefix)`** \u2014 new lookup added to the interface and all three implementations (Spring Data JPA `@Query`, JPA, and JDBC) so the set of colliding codes (`base` plus any `base-<n>`) can be fetched.\n- **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 a thin `findOwnersByCustomerCodeStartingWith` delegation, matching the existing facade methods.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.assignCustomerCode(owner)`** \u2014 a small private helper that generates the base code, fetches the taken codes, and returns the de-duplicated result, keeping `addOwner` readable.\n\nNo class became a catch-all; each piece has a single responsibility and reuses the existing generator, service, and repository patterns.",
